      "issueDetails": {
        "number": 2726,
        "title": "JndiLookup will not substitute environment variables when using an upper-case name",
        "body": "#### The Problem\n\nWhen using a lookup for an environment variable using `jndi:env/MY_VARIABLE` the lookup does not work when `MY_VARIABLE` is upper-case. The code in `JndiLookup` that normalizes the key by converting it to lower-case is incorrect.\n\n#### To Reproduce\n\n1. Define an environment variable `MY_VARIABLE=some_value`.\n2. Use the lookup `${jndi:env/MY_VARIABLE}` in `log4j2.xml`.\n3. The variable is not substituted.\n\nThis is a regression from previous versions.",
        "htmlUrl": "https://github.com/apache/logging-log4j2/issues/2726",
        "state": "open",
